{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/119813-baali-earthbound-vampire-what","id":119813,"title":"Baali: Earthbound, Vampire, What?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-26T10:20:08-07:00","id":119813,"title":"Baali: Earthbound, Vampire, What?","content":"ok..im confused...im running a crossover setting and i hear about a Baali clan..but i also know that Baali is a lesser earthbound..so...how should i pick it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T10:38:48-07:00","id":119822,"title":"","content":"Baal (not &quot;i&quot;) is a powerful earthbound. The Baali are a bloodline of vampires dealing with demonic entities and the &quot;Children&quot;, most likely the Neverborn. The two are not connected, unless you want them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T20:12:20-07:00","id":120693,"title":"","content":"I usually run with the idea that the Children are Neverborn. However, there is a way to link up the two different types of Infernalism (pre and post Demon the Fallen) and make it make sense in a general WoD setting. Both can be true without being mutually exclusive. Most of the &quot;Infernalism&quot; supplements are dealing with creatures that don't remotely resemble Demon the Fallen. The simplest way to make it all make sense is to say that pre-1999 most Infernalism dealt with Bane spirits taking on the roles of traditional demons, with the occasional summoning (ala Devil's Due) taking place. Post 1999 when the Rift opened, this other type of entity that almost no one had ever seen before started appearing. I have actually been planning an Infernalist hunting game set during this changeover as a plot point when all the known rules of Infernalism seem to be being broken by these new creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T21:02:02-07:00","id":120715,"title":"","content":"... I thought the canon (as much as there is one for cross-setting stuff, which gets a bit messy in cWoD) was that (virtually) all Demons anyone dealt with pre-Fallen were Earthbound, which are both significantly different from and much nastier than Fallen... but I'm not totally familiar with that particular aspect of the lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2836-nezumi","name":"Nezumi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T23:04:07-07:00","id":120778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nezumi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/119813-baali-earthbound-vampire-what?p=120715#post120715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I thought the canon (as much as there is one for cross-setting stuff, which gets a bit messy in cWoD) was that (virtually) all Demons anyone dealt with pre-Fallen were Earthbound, which are both significantly different from and much nastier than Fallen... but I'm not totally familiar with that particular aspect of the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon-canon, yes. Any other line...no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T05:40:29-07:00","id":120893,"title":"","content":"Baali is an archaic term for &quot;Lord&quot; in the archaic Babylonian language, the Earthbound context is talking about the Babylonian storm deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:14:53-07:00","id":121007,"title":"","content":"Coorection: Ba'al is a Canaanite word, not Babylonian. It's also more &quot;lord of this or that city&quot; more than just &quot;lord&quot;. Lord is &quot;El&quot;. Which is the &quot;al&quot; in Ba'al and is the end of the name of most of the angels. <br /> <br /> The Baal of the bible, which is the Baal that Vampire seems to be referencing when they start using the name and is definitely the one Demon is using from the Medieval demonology texts is usually Ba'al Hadad, about whom actually have some pretty cool pre-Bible myths. Look up &quot;Baal Cycle&quot; to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T14:41:26-07:00","id":121223,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected! I have only a passing familiarity with the ancient Middle East. Sumerian history and religion is the only thing I've done concrete studies on, with Marduk and Set being the two storm deities I'm most well versed in. <br /> <br /> Anywhom back on topic: Demon as a game line usually doesn't mesh too well with other games save for the occasional Faustian pact as a story element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":812,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","user":"Datura","date":". 04-28-2014, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T15:20:34-07:00","id":121254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anywhom back on topic: Demon as a game line usually doesn't mesh too well with other games save for the occasional Faustian pact as a story element. </div> </div> </div>This is an opinion I run into a lot and have never understood. I've been integrating Demon into my universal cosmology for games since it came out and have never really had problems. All you need to do is to establish what the other &quot;demons&quot; present in canon before its publication were and make that divide. I chose Bane spirits but they could just as easily be something else (Wyrm entities, Abyssal entities, Spectres, take your pick). That's about the only big problem for integration. So why do so many cry out that it is impossible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T16:27:14-07:00","id":121286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/119813-baali-earthbound-vampire-what?p=121254#post121254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So why do so many cry out that it is impossible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Au contraire, it's a far cry from impossible. In fact I think that some Demon factions, like the Cryptics for instance, can be integrated pretty well into an Occult-heavy chronicle, especially if you use Devil's Due and Earthbound (some of the better books for the classic World of Darkness in my opinion). <br /> <br /> With that said: Demon does have some parts that really turn off certain players. For one, Demon retconned quite a few already-established Demonic creatures into Earthbound. Couple that with the fact that Demon wrote off quite a few religious backdrops as just worshiping Earthbound puts off quite a few Storytellers and Players alike. Being a fan of Paradise Lost I did like Demon, but found that it isn't the best for crossovers unless you're willing to repress and remove certain aspects of it.<br /> <br /> As far as it fitting into the grand cosmology of cWoD: It fits decently, stilll with quite a few conflicts and kinks to iron out, with Vampire, Wraith, and Hunter, but as soon as you integrate it with Werewolf, Mage, or Changeling a wrench gets thrown into the cohesion of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T17:58:23-07:00","id":121333,"title":"","content":"My take on the Baali is that the 'Children' they serve/worship/protect are some kind of LIVING Neverborn, and the great Malfeans of the Labyrinth of <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> are the ghosts of those monsters... Which leans somewhat heavily on lore from the Underworld of <b>Exalted</b>, I understand. The Fallen, the Earthbound, all of those from <b>Demon</b> are different, but exactly as described in the books.<br /> <br /> As for <b>Demon</b> not playing well with other lines: Where it DOES fit, it's kinda neat. Kupala from <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> as an Earthbound in the Transylvanian basin is wonderful! Um, and that's about where the great fits end.<br /> <br /> By the bye (and really back on topic!), if one reads the <b>Dark Ages</b> book <i>Devil's Due</i>, it offers in the back an interesting way to incorporate the Baali with the Fallen, insomuch as the demons in that book align with <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T14:52:44-07:00","id":126160,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure the Children are whatever you want them to be, that is why they are never defined. Neverborn seems the most likely answer from any oWoD veteran. Baal is, as stated, an Earthbound Demon (of Demon the Fallen fame). Of course, as Phalon said, Devil's Due works wonders for incorporating DtF elements into Vampire when crossovers, or simple plot loan, are called for. However, given the Baali deal not only with Demons of &quot;The Inferno&quot;, but &quot;The Abyss&quot; and what might well be Malfeas... the Baali aren't limited to one specific brand of demonology. It is also worth mentioning that the term Ba'al is used as a placeholder by the ancient and elder Ba'ali. It means &quot;Lord&quot; and it is used as the True Names (or even Celestial Names) of Demons are highly valued and neither easily shared, nor foolishly spoken aloud in passing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}